  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acompa&#xF1;amiento integral a personas, organizaciones, y comunidades defensoras de DDHH en territorios de Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks organisational strengthening, comprehensive protection and the promotion of (self-) care actions for human rights defenders, especially women, ethnic and peasant communities and environmental defenders, in contexts of structural impunity and violations of the rule of law, aggravated by the environmental crisis in the regions of Colombia. PBI&apos;s accompaniment not only protects members of the organisations we accompany, but everyone in the communities and regions where we are indirectly present. This comprehensive accompaniment is fundamental for communities and organisations to be able to develop peacebuilding initiatives and projects in defence of human rights in a protected space. We also seek to make these initiatives and the situation of their promoters visible at a national and international level in order to achieve sustained support for them.
Our integral protection model is based on 4 complementary work axes: 1) the physical accompaniment and international observation of accompanied people and processes to generate safe working spaces; 2) the work of interlocution with Colombian civil and military entities at the national and regional level to convey concerns about the situation of our accompanied and accompanied people; and interlocution with allied and support network actors in the United States, Europe and Colombia, to support requests for the protection of accompanied people and communities, and to generate international pressure with the aim of achieving full respect for human rights; 3) the production and dissemination of communication materials to make visible and inform about the risks faced by human rights defenders; and 4) the reconstruction of the social fabric through the promotion and facilitation of spaces for meeting and collective construction of organised civil society, based on a comprehensive protection approach that includes security (physical and digital) and psychosocial support.</narrative>
  </description>
